<title>JAPAN: Japan March construction orders rise 6.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan March construction orders rise 6.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Orders received by 50 major Japanese construction companies rose 6.5 percent in March from a year earlier to 3.33 trillion yen, the Construction Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It was the first  rise in five months.</p>
<p>In February, orders fell 11.1 percent year-on-year to 1.32 trillion yen.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of overall construction orders in March (in yen, with year-ago percentage comparisons, all figures rounded):</p>
<p> Domestic private-sector orders    2.00 trln   +13.6 pct</p>
<p> Domestic public-sector orders     1.03 trln    -9.6 pct</p>
<p>Orders for foreign government facilities in Japan and orders</p>
<p>worth less than 10 million yen	   59.51 bln    -3.8 pct</p>
<p> Orders received abroad	     238.01 bln   +45.9 pct</p>
</text>
